# Change The Case Of The String With Methods

name = 'muzaffar hussain'
print(name.title())

o/p -> Muzaffar Hussain 

Here with the help of title() method we have converted the every word of string in title case .

A method is an action that python can perform on a piece of data.

dot(.) after the name in the name.title() tells python to make the title() method act on the variable name.


# Other methods also avaieble dealing with case 

print(name.upper()) -> converts each letter in the uppercase
print(name.lower()) -> converts each letter in the lower case 

